      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have heard that this problem is caused by the shader keyword system in Unity. \n\nTo properly apply PPS effects, the system uses certain keywords (i.e. BLOOM to enable bloom, BLOOM_LOW to enable fast mode bloom). However, Unity only supports a maximum of <255 keywords enabled at one time. \n\nThere are many possible shaders people can use for avatars, particle effects, and worlds. If these shaders are not designed with VRC in mind, they may use additional keywords. Once the limit is reached, further keywords can not be used.\n\nWhen new keywords can not be added, the incorrect shader variant will be used.\n\nThis problem can not be solved by VRC, but they could apply a workaround, such as initialising the PPS keywords when the game is launched for priority.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
