  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "An Emissive object placed in the world emits a dazzling light to a specific user, as if he were looking at the sun.\nUnbearable pain! ! !\nThe PPS threshold is 1.5. Emissive's material is HDR 3.\nIt occurs with either Directional Light, Bake, or Realtime.\nThere is no PointLight or SpotLight nearby. Light at a distant place is Bake.\nReflection Probe is installed in RealTime.\nThere is no LightProbe.\nIt may be improved by restarting VRChat and re-login.\nIt did not occur when you entered the world alone.\nThis happens to newcomers who join a world where many people have already stayed.\nThis bug only happens in the view of the user.\nI can not feel it to other people.\nPeople who occur frequently.\nThe person who does not occur does not occur at all.\n\nIt is unlikely that the avatar may have a defect with Shader.\nVRChat side has failed to compile PPS?\n\nThis problem has existed for more than half a year.\n\nThe wonder of PPS that may be related.\nBloom is working. However, there are users who do not work with Color Grading.",
